 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "Stress testing in “Bank Melli Iran” Baku Branch:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "In order to manage the liquidity risks, the branch prepares stress testing and scenarios on each liquidity risks along with the risk map and sensitivity analysis."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "Stress tests and scenarios allow determining the effect of micro and macro scale changes on the balance sheet and off-balance sheet assets and obligations of the branch."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "This stress testing allows clarifying the losses which may be in the emergency market conditions."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "The procedure of the implementation of stress testing:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "Firstly, the accuracy of the data is checked and data basis are determined."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "Secondly, risks are determined for the implementation of stress testing."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "These risks:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Interest",
    "Liquidity",
    "Credit",
    "Currency"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "In this case stress testing can be carried out in two types:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": true,
   "items": [
    "Stress testing on scenarios",
    "Sensitivity testing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "Scenarios are determined and the reasons of the selection of scenarios are shown. These scenarios are selected by taking into account the historical data."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "The results are compared. The specific measures are carried out."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "During sensitivity testing the sensitive assets and obligations are taken into account, measured and planned. Sensitive assets and liabilities mean the measurement in private of sensitivity of balance sheet ad off-balance sheet assets and obligations. This sensitivity analysis is important for the proper planning of liquidity. This analysis is used for the calculation of Value at Risk and the preparation of scenarios."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "html": "2 main goals are put while carrying out stress testing:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": true,
   "items": [
    "Checking of capital adequacy for the payment of possible losses",
    "Determination of weak points in order to increase risks and maintain capital and elimination of them"
   ]
  },
